(function(payload){if(typeof applySerialChapterPayload==="function")applySerialChapterPayload(payload);else (window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE||(window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE=[])).push(payload);})({"id":"serial-cultivation-31","version":"0a6b940755c1","book":"mountain-ledger","cn":["沈砚没有一笔随手可花的[[fortune|财富]]，季禾将听水筒的[[receiver|接收端]]贴上老井。海边[[hurricane|飓风]]带来的雨云使风声很[[loud|大]]，他需分辨井侧是否还通清泉。祭司说得[[fluent|流利]]，指向井旁新[[bud|芽]]：这里一直有湿气，不是全干。守井人愿交出副钥匙，免去取水的[[freedom|自由]]不能只赏给认识掌事的人。整扇[[substantial|厚实的]]柜门挡住阀件，原来装在掌事的[[wardrobe|衣柜]]里。守库人被叫成[[gangster|打手]]，沈砚仍请他先出示入库单，不拿骂名当证据。","罗清给患者的解释[[sincere|诚恳]]，抄一张[[leaflet|告示]]说明水车几时到，没让清泉的[[glamour|魅力]]掩住风险。庙中[[religious|宗教的]]捐罐先用[[cork|软木塞]]封好，[[golden|金色的]]供灯照着一枚[[jewel|宝石]]，烛火使它[[glitter|闪闪发光]]。沈砚不动捐资柜，祭司却愿将临时租金从自己那份香火钱出。他要求旧单的[[grammatical|文法上的]]原句不改，清水不是“可随意取尽”。两人[[scan|细看]]原刻，发现每天余量要先保井边住户，远来的救急队也不能把他们的水带空。","井边[[vegetation|草木]]留着长期水线，守井人按[[habitual|惯常的]]巡视路线领路。陶溯让伙计以[[dictation|口授]]改告示，要[[announce|宣布]]破坏公用井的人自负灾祸。远处[[wolf|狼]]叫让小工吓住，季禾守在[[arch|拱门]]旁，说先听井，不听吓唬。沈砚希望的[[democracy|民众共议]]不只是排满人头，已有[[asleep|睡着的]]住户也应明天能看记录。为了[[inspire|鼓励]]他们，他先把有水有量的旧告示放回[[bald|光秃的]]门石上，借[[wool|毛线]]绑住纸角，夜风再大也别吹成空白。","五户以豆子作[[ballot|选票]]选看水人，动作很[[awkward|笨拙]]，却没有谁替沉默者投。一位穿[[blouse|宽松上衣]]的妇人很[[impatient|急切]]，她家本就短水，要求医馆别拿尽。庙里旧[[boiler|煮水锅]]可容几罐，近[[fortnight|两星期]]却被封着。季禾用[[bough|粗树枝]]支住坏门，许庭像[[lord|领主]]般发话，妇人将空[[bowl|碗]]摆到他面前：要说带走多少，先说给这里留下多少。驮水的[[beast|牲口]]也需喝水，不能把账写得只有货。沈砚把这个消耗一同列出，商量每次车队只取井的剩余量。","山泉的一条[[branch|支流]]通向庙后，祭司作出开阀的[[gesture|手势]]，井口的[[brightness|光亮]]映上水面。许庭先问自己能得多少[[interest|利息]]，沈砚请他[[browse|查看]]租约，水源不计息。他作为[[critic|挑剔者]]抱怨不少，却亲手给锅底[[burner|火炉]]添柴，因为他也要这条货路继续。看水人、医馆与祭司共同[[constitute|组成]]临时管水组，季禾清除遮口的[[bush|灌木]]，让人人看得见阀。清水没有在一刻间让疾病消失，但井边妇人拿到第一碗，才允许水车去城里；这碗不是赏给她的，是本来属于她的份。","水车到医馆已过子时，沈砚肩上的绳勒出血印。他把首车水量交给罗清，没说如今一切安全；她核对封口与来源，分给急需者，并持续记录。第二车留在城南，不能只救他们守着的一间馆。许庭催租金，沈砚按约付首日，又把还款与调水分别贴出。天亮顾衡的回信到了：补给队已离山，周伯带两个学徒守渠。沈砚最想听到的仍是家里水位没掉。他看着路口等第二车回来，明天要去追阀件的拆运单，不能让今日勉强成立的供水再被一句坏了收走。"],"en":["Without spare [[fortune|fortune]], Shen watched Ji place a listening tube’s [[receiver|receiver]] against the well. Rain from a coastal [[hurricane|hurricane]] made wind [[loud|loud]]. The priest gave [[fluent|fluent]] directions to a wet [[bud|bud]]. The keeper lent a key: drawing [[freedom|freedom]] should not depend on knowing Tao. A [[substantial|substantial]] door hid valve parts in a [[wardrobe|wardrobe]]. Shen requested an inventory from the keeper rather than treating the label [[gangster|gangster]] as proof.","Luo offered [[sincere|sincere]] explanations and a [[leaflet|leaflet]] with arrival times, not the [[glamour|glamour]] of guaranteed pure water. [[religious|Religious]] donation jars received [[cork|cork]] seals. A [[golden|golden]] lamp made a [[jewel|jewel]] [[glitter|glitter]]. Shen left donation funds alone; the priest offered his own share for rent. They preserved the [[grammatical|grammatical]] limits of old notices. To [[scan|scan]] them revealed local households had priority; the rescue party could not empty their well.","[[vegetation|Vegetation]] marked old waterlines along the keeper’s [[habitual|habitual]] route. Tao ordered a changed notice by [[dictation|dictation]], planning to [[announce|announce]] that openers owed all disasters. A [[wolf|wolf]] frightened workers. Ji stood at the [[arch|arch]] and directed them towards actual water. Shen’s [[democracy|democracy]] included [[asleep|asleep]] households able to read tomorrow. To [[inspire|inspire]] participation, he returned the measured notice to a [[bald|bald]] stone and secured it with [[wool|wool]].","Five households used beans as a [[ballot|ballot]], [[awkward|awkward]] but independent. A woman in a [[blouse|blouse]] was [[impatient|impatient]] about her own shortage. A [[boiler|boiler]] had been locked for a [[fortnight|fortnight]]. Ji propped its door with a [[bough|bough]]. Xu spoke like a [[lord|lord]] until the woman set an empty [[bowl|bowl]] before him: how much would remain? The carrying [[beast|beast]] needed water too. Shen recorded that cost and agreed that carts would take only measured surplus.","A spring [[branch|branch]] reached behind the temple. The priest’s [[gesture|gesture]] opened a valve into [[brightness|brightness]]. Xu requested [[interest|interest]]; Shen asked him to [[browse|browse]] the hire terms, which did not mortgage water. An active [[critic|critic]], Xu nevertheless fed the [[burner|burner]] because trade required this route. Local watchers, healers and priest would [[constitute|constitute]] a temporary group. Ji removed a [[bush|bush]] so the valve was visible. The woman received her rightful first bowl before the carts left. Water did not instantly end illness.","After midnight Shen brought the first load, rope cuts on his shoulders. Luo checked seals and sources before distributing it and continued observations. The second cart served the south district. Shen paid Xu’s first rent and posted accounts separately from water figures. Gu’s message arrived: supplies had left home while Zhou and two apprentices kept the channel. Shen wanted assurance that village levels held. Tomorrow he must trace removal orders so today’s fragile supply could not again disappear under a claim of broken parts."]});
